Allright that's my second ascension! A Weaponless Vegetarian Monk, no less. 
I should stop playing for a while, I stopped for a few weeks after my first
and now I'm hooked again ;-)

Everything below, from before the astral planes is from memory and may not
be 100% accurate. I don't keep notes.
Again it's probably overly long...  I suck at doing these write-ups.

What's notable was what was missing: I never found a BoH or a ?oCharging.
Only one ?oGenocide and /oWishing.
After having done Sokoban and the Mines, things weren't looking that great.
I had no decent armor, my pet died. Had found only one ?iIdentify and was
generally miserable.
That all changed when I found a figurine of an Archon a few levels below
Sokoban. I had only ever met a few Archons, so i had no idea how useful
they are. (except it was a high level monster) I applied it and I had a new
pet. Archons are amazing I had a stethoscope and after I checked it I was
_very_ impressed (don't recall the numbers, but I was pleased!).
So much so that after seeing it wielded an artifact weapon, doesn't eat and
heals itself. Seeing it in action I decided keeping this pet around was my
no 1. priority.

That was also when my luck changed, I found a few thrones 5 IIRC all
granting wishes, one of them just kept going and going (only one wish) but
I sat on it for maybe 40 times and it gave me two genocides lots of create
monsters which was fun and a couple stat increases (Charisma?).

One other notable thing was that !of Healing were smokey, I got a couple of
wishes off them too, all in all I wished for Gauntlets of Power/ Hem of
Brilliance and a Bag of Holding in the beginning of the game.
Another Archon Figurine and a Magic Whistle when I got frustrated herding
them up the stairs.
End game I wished for a few spellbooks as I was getting quite spoiled, I
believe Identify/ Magic Mapping and Stone to Flesh (As I didn't find
any !oAcid and didn't want to have to eat a lizard).

The rest of the game was pretty uneventful actually, the Wizard double
troubled me only once.
I zapped a few elf lords to death mistaking them for the wizard...
Had some trouble with the mysterious force on levels 42 (5 times) and 38
(even more, I lost count.) But after that only two more times.
The malignent aura was no problem, I had remove curse.



The final run on the planes went something like this:
Earth.
Cakewalk.
Apparently I should not have relied on magic mapping to find the portals.
Confused gold detection did the trick, but I thought Magic Mapping would
work. 
The wizard showed up twice, went down to a /oDeath both times.


Air:
I don't remember getting such a beating by the engulfing attack of the air
elementals last time. After exhausting 2 wands of teleport on getting them
off my back I settled on /oDeath to zap them when engulfed.
I had wanted to save them for astral...
Half way developed the tactic of hiding inside vortices, should've thought
of that before.


Fire:
Lucky, the portal was maybe 10-15 paces away. 
Dove into a vortex, whistled my pets in when I got expelled I was at 100%
hitpoints and my pets had taken care of at least 4 incoming E's. ;-)
After a quick check of the cursedness of the inventory the three of us dove
into the portal just before an incoming Archon could reach us.


Water:
It got a lot easier than last time, or rather: more comfortable.
I still don't understand how this level works. I learned since the previous
time that allthough it looks like you're floating inside a bubble you
_cannot_ go outside the bubble wearing waterwalking boots. (So i threw
those out of my backpack). But you can using levitation, duh.. Seems
inconsistent with my bubble theory but that's how it is...
I got the idea that it should be possible, due to my Archon pets moving
about freely outside the bubble.
Last time I was freaked out about the prospect of drowning everytime the
bubble closed in on me.
And don't get me started on the way the portal moves about, I lost it twice
while making final preparations. I just float around in my bubble until I
find it again. There probably is a better way, but I have no clue how I
could do it more intelligently. 
The portal probably moves around within one of the not-quite-bubbles, but
I'm not sure.

After that little mystery solved, the rest was fairly uneventful. Two Archon
pets make for a great team of body guards.
After that I made good use of the magic markers I still had, blanked some
useless scrolls, wrote enchant armor and enchanted all armor to it's
maximum. I was holding out for a scoll of charging so I could recharge some
useful wands, but I never found one. (Stupid me now remmebers I wished for
one in the castle and could have written them, I must have missed them
while reviewing the known scrolls)
I Got out some food, dumped some crap form the inventory, waited for the
portal to show up again, whistled my body guards in, and dove into the
portal... 


